@startuml
title Document Management (ERC-1643) — Native vs External Engine
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

package "Pattern A — Native storage (all variants except Light)" {
  [CMTAT token\n+ DocumentERC1643Module] as A
  database "ERC-7201 storage\n_documents / _documentNames" as ADB
  A --> ADB : setDocument / removeDocument\n[DOCUMENT_ROLE]
}

package "Pattern B — External engine (optional module)" {
  [CMTAT token\n+ DocumentEngineModule] as B
  [DocumentEngine\n(IERC1643)] as ENG
  database "Engine storage" as BDB
  B --> ENG : forwards get / set / remove\n[DOCUMENT_ENGINE_ROLE]
  ENG --> BDB
}

note bottom
  Both expose getDocument / getAllDocuments / setDocument / removeDocument
  with bytes32 document names. Native ships in every variant except Light;
  the external engine keeps the token lean and can serve many tokens.
end note
@enduml
